--- Estimates the number of slots in a vtable by walking entries until one fails a validity check. An entry is considered valid when it is non-null, in the range `0x10000`–`0x7FFFFFFFFFFF`, and points to executable memory. The walk stops at the first invalid or inaccessible entry.
--- @param vtbl number Address of the vtable (not the object).
--- @return number R1 Estimated number of slots.
function ffi.vtable.size(vtbl) end --- @diagnostic disable-line

--- Locates the vtable for a named C++ class inside a loaded module using RTTI metadata. The search follows the standard MSVC RTTI chain:
--- 
--- 1. Scans `.data` for the `TypeDescriptor` matching `.?AV<name>@@`.
--- 2. Scans `.rdata` for the `CompleteObjectLocator` that references it.
--- 3. Scans `.rdata` for the vftable meta-pointer that references the locator.
--- 4. Returns the address of the slot immediately after the meta-pointer, which is the first virtual method slot.
--- 
--- Returns `nil` if any step fails (class not found, stripped RTTI, or the module lacks `.data`/`.rdata` sections).
--- @param handle lightuserdata Module handle (e.g. from `lje.module.get`).
--- @param name string Undecorated class name as it appears in the RTTI type descriptor, e.g. `"MyClass"`.
--- @return number? R1 Address of the vtable's first slot, or `nil` if the class could not be located.
function ffi.vtable.find(handle, name) end --- @diagnostic disable-line

--- Finds live instances of a class by scanning memory for the vtable pointer. The vtable address is resolved first via RTTI (same as `find`). The scan proceeds in two phases:
--- 
--- 1. **Module `.data` section** — fast, covers most static/global instances.
--- 2. **Process-wide memory scan** — falls back to this only when no results are found in phase 1. Scans all read-write, non-image memory regions that are at least `min_size` bytes large.
--- 
--- Each result is the address where the vtable pointer was found — i.e. the likely start of an object of that class.
--- 
--- Returns an empty table (never `nil`) when the vtable cannot be found or no matches exist.
--- @param handle lightuserdata Module handle (e.g. from `lje.module.get`).
--- @param name string Undecorated class name, e.g. `"MyClass"`.
--- @param multiple boolean? If `true`, collect all matches in phase 1 instead of stopping at the first. Defaults to `false`.
--- @param min_size number? Minimum region size (bytes) for the process-wide phase-2 scan. Defaults to `1048576` (1 MB).
--- @return table R1 Array of addresses (numbers) where the vtable pointer was found, ordered by discovery. May be empty.
function ffi.vtable.find_instances(handle, name, multiple, min_size) end --- @diagnostic disable-line